  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This game has had this issue since day 1 and NOTHING has seemingly been done to fix it. Its at the point, where I can't go to a public world or a friends plus without my avatar just being yoinked and uploaded to ripperstore or some other site. It really saddens me as I want to show off my avatars, I want to feel proud of the hard work I have put in it. At this point though I'm done using highly custom made avatars because its just going to be stolen anyways and the devs don't acknowledge it. They don't try to sue ripperstore for breaking TOS or anything. Its their job as a developer to make sure the community is safe from hackers, who cares about things like face tracking, and eye tracking when security has been their biggest issue and they decide to ignore it rather than fix it. Its easier than ever now to rip avatars its not even funny how many tools the developers of ripperstore got. They could easily be taken down as they are breaking not just VRChat TOS, but Unity, Patreon, Booth, Gumroad, Github, etc. Yet NOT A SINGLE PERSON CAN SEEM TO DO ANYTHING, they are not some \"archive\" site, if it was they wouldn't be distributing assets. They are straight up a piracy site, I love this game, I want to keep playing it for years to come. However myself and others including streamers and various content creators and players and communities are sick and tired of our avatars just being stolen and the VRC devs only just ban a user, that doesnt fix the fact that person can make another account and just reupload the model or share it on a site. Even the ripperstore devs themselves had said its not hard to make the security better, VRC just doesn't do it for whatever reason. I know its not gonna be a 100% fix, but by making it way harder for them to do, would be better than ignoring it in the first place.",
